# Generated visual previews and spreadsheet inspection diagnostics
outputs/**/overview-preview.png
outputs/**/register-preview.png
outputs/**/rwt-row-preview.png
outputs/**/*.inspect.ndjson

# Local RimWorld build products
bin/
obj/
Assemblies/*.dll
Assemblies/*.pdb
*.log

# Machine-local tooling, package caches, decompiled reference inspection, build evidence.
#
# The 40 register PROOFS and the 11 PLANT suites are the exception, un-ignored below. Owner
# direction, 2026-09-30, verbatim: *"i need someone else to work on this in parrellel through
# git hub and i need to make sure they have it all but the temp stuff i told you to git ignore"*.
# Those scripts are neither machine-local nor temp -- they are this project's primary
# verification instrument, and a clone without them can run the 13 checkers and none of the 40
# proofs. Everything else under .local/ stays out: a 132 MB nuget cache, 19 MB of decompiler
# binaries, the per-subsystem source inspections, and the one-shot record/ship/fix scripts.
#
# Git does not descend into an ignored directory, so the parent has to be re-admitted a level
# at a time before a negation inside it can match. Same pattern as !.claude/bin/ below.
.local/*
!.local/register/
.local/register/*
!.local/register/proof-*.py
!.local/register/plant-*.py
artifacts/
Mod/**/Assemblies/*.dll
Mod/**/Assemblies/*.pdb
*.local.props

# Local editor state and machine-specific game profiles
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
**/ModsConfig.xml
**/ModConfig.json

# Generic dependency, cache, temp and log noise (never ship-worthy)
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.cache/
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak

# Claude Code workflow (.claude/) IS tracked in this repository — owner decision 2026-09-28,
# both remotes verified PRIVATE (see docs/FINALIZED.md). Only machine-local session state
# and personal files inside it stay out of git.
.claude/.session-env.json
.claude/.session-state.md
.claude/.session-tidbits.md
.claude/.last-session.md
.claude/.session-usage.jsonl
.claude/.usage-tracking-disabled
.claude/.yolo-mode
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.env
.claude/user.json
.claude/user-context/
# The generic bin/ rule above is for .NET output; the workflow's bundled scanner binaries ship
!.claude/bin/
